    "lawCode": "Amd §89-c, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3789\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to authorizing the\npublic service commission to require water-works corporations to provide\ncertain residents with non-billing related information\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would require waterworks corporations to provide non-billing\nrelated information to water users that reside in condominiums, cooper-\natives or certain multi-family residences.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends the public service law, as it relates to\nduiring waterworks companies to prove certain non-billing information\nsuch as service updates and water quality notices to certain residents\nwhose cater is distributed by a master meter.\n\nSection 2 of the bill relates to the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nResidents who live in certain condominiums, cooperatives or multi-family\nresidences are not afforded the same access to critical information on\ntheir water that other users are. These residents receive their water\nthrough a master meter and ,:re not considered customers by the water-\nworks corporations. As a result, they do not directly receive any\nnotifications regarding water quality or service interruptions. This\nbill empowers the public service commission to require waterworks corpo-\nrations create a process where these residents are able to obtain non-\nbilling related information regarding their water.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
